; The questions about the oversight system, kept next to the model (§16).

; Can the case ever conclude at all? (§16.1 `possible` — and, holding, it now
; prints the shortest route that concludes the docket.)
(property conviction-possible
  "the docket can conclude"
  (possible (is docket.stage concluded)))

; Can ONE lawful move permanently destroy accountability? `live` asks whether a
; concluded docket is still reachable from EVERY reachable situation. It holds
; here because restore-watchdog can always undo a capture, so the prosecutor can
; regain independence and the case can still conclude.
(property accountability
  "the docket can always still conclude"
  (live (is docket.stage concluded)))

; Which of our own powers can violate our own declared law? `pol check` reports
; that same-agency can be broken by capture-watchdog and restore-watchdog (both
; write watchdog.independence, an arrow the same-agency routes traverse). We
; acknowledge exactly those two — recording ownership (§16.3). We do NOT accept
; conclude or assign-judge: neither writes an arrow on either route, so an
; accept on them would be reported `stale`.
(accept capture-watchdog same-agency)
(accept restore-watchdog same-agency)

; Which bureaus are captured right now? (§16.2)
(query captured-bureaus
  (where (b bureau))
  (is b.independence captured))
